      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:7:7:2:4",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) الْيَمِينُ الصَّبْرُ الْكَاذِبَةُ تُورِثُ الْعَقِبَ الْفَقْرَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from hannan, from Fuleyh Bin Abu Bakr Al Shaybani who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The impatient false oath inherits the consequence of poverty’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from Fianan from Fulayh ibn abu Bakr al-Shaybaniy who has narrated the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Taking an oath which is false and binding causes poverty consequently.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
